### What is lock downgrading?

A `ReentrantReadWriteLock` exposes `readLock()` (shared) and `writeLock()` (exclusive). The holder of the write lock can also acquire the read lock because the lock is reentrant.

### How do you downgrade?

```java
ReentrantReadWriteLock rw = new ReentrantReadWriteLock();

rw.writeLock().lock();                 // exclusive
try {
    rate = newRate;                    // WRITE
    rw.readLock().lock();              // acquire read BEFORE releasing write
} finally {
    rw.writeLock().unlock();           // now only read held: downgrade complete
}
try {
    return applyRate(rate);            // READ the fresh value safely
} finally {
    rw.readLock().unlock();
}
```

### Why is upgrading forbidden?

If a thread holds the read lock and calls `writeLock().lock()`, it blocks because the write lock needs exclusivity but the thread itself still holds a read lock. Two threads both upgrading deadlock.

```java
// DEADLOCK RISK:
rw.readLock().lock();
try {
    rw.writeLock().lock();   // blocks forever: waiting for own read lock
} finally { /* ... */ }
```

### What is the upgrade workaround?

Release read, acquire write, re-check the condition.

```java
rw.readLock().lock();
try {
    if (needsUpdate(rate)) {
        rw.readLock().unlock();        // release read first
        rw.writeLock().lock();         // acquire write
        try {
            if (needsUpdate(rate)) {   // re-check: state may have changed!
                rate = computeNewRate();
            }
            rw.readLock().lock();      // downgrade
        } finally {
            rw.writeLock().unlock();
        }
    }
    return applyRate(rate);
} finally {
    rw.readLock().unlock();
}
```

### Why is downgrading useful?

It closes the race window. Without it, releasing write then separately acquiring read lets another writer change the value in between.

| Approach | Race Window? | Continuity? |
|----------|-------------|-------------|
| Downgrade (read before releasing write) | No | Guaranteed |
| Release write, then acquire read | Yes | Not guaranteed |

### What are common interview follow-up questions?

- How does StampedLock handle optimistic reads and upgrades?
- Can you downgrade from a StampedLock write stamp to a read stamp?
- What pattern replaces upgrade in practice?
